<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10852" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contortĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		contorqueo. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A whirling round</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dexterae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4</span></i>
			, 
			 19, 26 <i>fin.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An intertwining, involving; intricacy,
			complication;</i> of discourse, in the plur.:
			contortiones orationis, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Fat. 9,
				17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. Retract. 1, 50</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
